    "summary": "High‑energy Oakland ’82 with smoking Throwing Stones→Franklin’s Tower",
    "review": "December 30, 1982 at the Oakland Auditorium Arena was a straight‑up fire‑cracker of a night. The band hit top gear from the opening “Alabama Getaway” and kept the momentum rolling through a setlist that mixed new ’82 material with classic staples. Highlights include an early “Touch of Grey,” the monster Throwing Stones → Franklin’s Tower segue (the kind of tight transition that makes you grin all night), Brent’s sparkling keys on Franklin’s, and the horn‑fueled double encore of “Hard To Handle” and “Tell Mama.” The second set kept the groove alive with a soaring “Saint Of Circumstance,” a tambourine‑dancing Billy behind Mickey’s standout drum solo in “He’s Gone,” and a jubilant run through “Truckin’,” “Stella Blue,” and “Johnny B. Goode.” Across all recordings the energy stays sky‑high, making this a must‑listen for anyone who loves that early‑’80s Dead magic.",
